  "full_text": "This is a little song from Black Sabbath called Trashed by Jesus Christ himself, Ian Gillen. It was really a meeting. The bottle took a beating. The ladies in the manor watched me climb into my car about, and I was going down a track about 105. I had the stopwatch roaring. I had the headlights blazing. I was really alive, and yet my mind was blowing. I drank a bottle of tequila, and I feel real good. Had the tape deck roaring. But on the 25th lap, I hit a canal turn. I went off exploring, and I knew I wouldn't make it. The car just wouldn't take it. I was turning, tires burning. The ground was in my sky. I was laughing. The bitch was trashed, and death was in my eye. I'd started pretty good and I was feeling my way. I had the wheels in motion. There was Peter in the green flying, laughing like drains. Inebriation. The crowd was roaring. I was hand branched. I had my imagination. But at the canal turn, I hit an oily patch. Inebriation. Oh, Mr. Miracle, you saved me from some pain. Thank you, Mr. Miracle. I won't get trashed again. Can you hear my lies? Don't you bother with this fool. Just laugh into my eyes. So we went back to the bar and in a bottle again, there's no tequila. Then we started on no whiskey just to steady our brains, cause there was no tequila. And as we drank a little faster at the top of our hill, we began to roar. And as we got dressed, we started laughing still. Well, bless my soul.",
